+# Research
+
+## Request paths and current behavior
+
+- `ProductApi.delete` delegates `DELETE /api/v1/private/product/{id}` to `ProductCommonFacadeImpl.deleteProduct`, which calls `ProductServiceImpl.delete`. Product deletion removes catalog-owned data and the product row. `ShoppingCartItem.product` is `@Transient`; the persisted cart line keeps `PRODUCT_ID` and `SKU`, so deletion does not cascade through a JPA product association.
+- Cart retrieval goes through `ShoppingCartServiceImpl.getByCode/getById`, then `getPopulatedShoppingCart`. Each line is reloaded by SKU in `getPopulatedItem`. If the product no longer exists, the line is only marked `obsolete`; the containing cart is marked obsolete, and the public getter deletes/returns `null`. This is the direct cause of carts becoming unreadable.
+- `ShoppingCartDataPopulator` and `ReadableShoppingCartMapper` dereference `item.getProduct()` and calculate from the cart lines. They are safe only after missing lines have been removed from the model. Totals are recalculated by `ShoppingCartCalculationService`, so the remaining lines must be the source of truth.
+- Cart mutation creates new lines through `ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.createCartItem`/`createCartItems`, which resolve products by SKU. Missing products currently become generic exceptions in the single-item path and `ResourceNotFoundException` in the multi-item path; the API contract requires a consistent HTTP 404.
+- Checkout (`OrderFacadeImpl.processOrderModel`) resolves every cart line by SKU and rejects missing products. Therefore checkout will work after deleted lines are removed during cart hydration, but must not receive an obsolete line.
+
+## Orders
+
+- `OrderProduct` stores the purchased SKU, product name, ordered quantity and one-time charge, with order-product prices and attributes also stored independently. There is no product association to break when the catalog product is deleted.
+- `ReadableOrderProductMapper` and the deprecated `ReadableOrderProductPopulator` already populate the required SKU, name, quantity, price and subtotal from the `OrderProduct` snapshot, then optionally enrich `ReadableOrderProduct.product` by looking up the current SKU. The enrichment is conditional on a product being found, so deleted products should remain representable from the snapshot; all order response paths need to continue using this behavior without requiring a live product.
+- Order loading uses `OrderRepository.findOne` and the custom list queries, which fetch `OrderProduct` and its prices/attributes rather than joining to catalog products. The order totals are stored on `Order` and are not recalculated by these reads. Status updates use the order id and do not need the product row.
+- The merchant/customer order facade paths build response products from `OrderProduct`; the v0 merchant path additionally uses the deprecated populator. Both need to preserve snapshot data and avoid any null live-product dereference.
+
+## Product lookup
+
+- `ProductApiV2.get("/api/v2/product/{sku}")` calls `ProductFacadeV2.getProductByCode`. The v2 facade already translates a missing SKU (or wrong store) to `ResourceNotFoundException`, so the existing endpoint behavior is HTTP 404 and needs no product-deletion-specific change.
+
+## Files likely affected
+
+- `sm-core/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/core/business/services/shoppingcart/ShoppingCartServiceImpl.java`: remove missing-product cart lines, retain the cart even when empty, and persist the cleaned line set.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/mapper/cart/ReadableShoppingCartMapper.java` and/or the deprecated cart populator: tolerate/avoid missing lines and ensure empty carts expose zero products/quantity/totals.
+- `sm-shop/src/main/java/com/salesmanager/shop/store/controller/shoppingCart/facade/ShoppingCartFacadeImpl.java`: return `ResourceNotFoundException` for deleted SKUs in single and multi add/update flows.
+- No v2 product lookup change is needed: `ProductFacadeV2Impl` already maps a missing SKU to 404.
+- Order mapper/populator/facade code only if tests expose a live-product dereference; the persisted `OrderProduct` snapshot is the required source for deleted-product order output.
+
+## Verification targets
+
+- Existing unit/integration tests under `sm-shop/src/test`, especially cart, product, and order API integration tests.
+- Add focused regression coverage if the repository's test setup permits it: cart with deleted line plus surviving line, cart with only deleted line, add deleted SKU, all order read endpoints/status update, checkout, v2 deleted SKU, and an unrelated product.
